<h3>Plugin Builder Results</h3>

Congratulations! You just built a processing plugin for QGIS!<br/><br/>

<div id='help' style='font-size:.9em;'>
Your plugin <b>${TemplateClass}</b> was created in:<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>${PluginDir}</b>
<p>
Your QGIS plugin directory is located at:<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>${UserPluginDir}</b>
<p>
<h3>What's Next</h3>
<ol>
    <li>Add a <b>metadata.txt</b> to your plugin directory &mdash; QGIS requires it to load the plugin.</li>
    <li>Deploy the plugin using <b>pb_tool</b>:<br>
        <code>pb_tool deploy</code></li>
    <li>Enable the plugin in the QGIS Plugin Manager.</li>
    <li>Open the Processing Toolbox &mdash; your provider will appear under <b>${TemplateClass}</b>.</li>
    <li>Customise the algorithm by editing <b>${TemplateModuleName}_algorithm.py</b>.</li>
    <li>Add more algorithms by creating additional <b>QgsProcessingAlgorithm</b> subclasses and
        registering them in <b>${TemplateModuleName}_provider.py</b>.</li>
    <li>Create a custom icon by replacing the default <b>icon.png</b> and referencing it
        in your provider's <b>icon()</b> method.</li>
</ol>
<h3>File Overview</h3>
<ul>
    <li><b>${TemplateModuleName}.py</b> &mdash; Main plugin class; registers the processing provider with QGIS.</li>
    <li><b>${TemplateModuleName}_provider.py</b> &mdash; QgsProcessingProvider subclass; loads your algorithms.</li>
    <li><b>${TemplateModuleName}_algorithm.py</b> &mdash; Example QgsProcessingAlgorithm with input and output layers.</li>
    <li><b>__init__.py</b> &mdash; Plugin entry point required by QGIS.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div style='font-size:.9em;'>
<p>
For information on writing PyQGIS processing algorithms, see the
<a href='https://docs.qgis.org/latest/en/docs/pyqgis_developer_cookbook/'>PyQGIS Developer Cookbook</a>
and the <a href='https://qgis.org/pyqgis/master/core/QgsProcessingAlgorithm.html'>QgsProcessingAlgorithm API docs</a>.
</p>
</div>
